## Context and authority

Filed from replicator 0003 (branch t0003-full-chain, commit df890ef) at the
author's request. Integration-review finding for tracker 1552. Related:
1570 (probe and sign-off modes), 1569 (identification review), 1568
(independent confirmation). Request for receiving Imagine, not an
implementation authorization.

## Evidence

A blind full-chain pilot (assess, reproduce, probe, report) ran unattended
on two I4R papers with R packages, Weschle (2024, AJPS) and Atanasov et
al. (2024, EJ). The skill ran as installed at harness 04d8cf2 and 2360e75.
The robustness plan was signed by a two-seat panel (gpt-6-astra and
claude-fable-5-2) under an author ruling. Each folder was frozen and
audited for blindness, then compared with the I4R report on criteria
fixed before any fetch. Protocol, results and comparisons:
`~/CNRS/projets/actifs/replicator/replications/chain-pilot-0003/` (PROTOCOL.md, RESULTS.md,
*-comparison.md/json, *-blindness-audit.md). Paper folders:
`~/CNRS/projets/actifs/replicator/replications/weschle2024politicians/`,
`~/CNRS/projets/actifs/replicator/replications/atanasov2024taste/` (each has DEVIATIONS.md).

Both main results reproduce to the printed digit. All pilot pass criteria
are met; Atanasov's "no miss a rule should have caught" criterion is
borderline. No reproducibility-table disagreement with I4R is attributed
to the skill. These are two papers, not an accuracy estimate.

## Findings (as numbered in RESULTS.md)

1. Merge audit: check each merge's match rate on the code's own keys before any cleaning, and trace missing values in constructed variables.
2. Construction sweep: compare each variable definition and sample rule in the text and notes with the code.
3. Count a result asserted without numbers or code as not "already in the paper", both in `probe` and in the panel prompt.
4. Main-result selection has no rule; Weschle's executor had to set one.
5. Whether footnote results count as outputs is open, and the ACRe level depends on it (Atanasov: L5 or `non_etabli`).
6. Environment: the project's R image cannot build 2022–23 packages. Both executors built a digest-pinned image with the authors' R version.
7. The I4R General template prints 2 decimals; rule 2 requires 3.
8. An executor must not drop a signed check. Weschle's executor dropped F-P3 when a seat's condition could not be met.
9. A final report must never leave a table row blank. Weschle's raw-data row was left empty.
10. Monte Carlo noise and typos in quoted numbers should not alone make "reproducible from analysis data" Partially.
11. Consent for a cross-family reviewer of the identification review is unclear. Atanasov's executor added an identification section unprompted and skipped the cross-family review.
12. Panel sign-off worked mechanically on both papers (two rounds, no unreachable seat). Its rejections cost coverage against I4R in both papers (finding 3).

