## Author ruling: generic approval modes

Recorded 2026-11-27T11:42Z, relayed by the author’s own interface session /root. The
parent proposed two modes: (1) author approval in the plan file or in
conversation, with provenance-bearing transcription; (2) explicit author
delegation to a panel for a defined campaign and fixed perimeter, preserving
opinions/disagreements, without permanent general panel authority.

Actual author reply as relayed:

> Oui, deux modes. Le skill est générique, replicator est le driver principal à ce jour mais l’année prochaine on pourrait en avoir d’autre. Par exemple un auto-blog, une veille scientifique, une métaanalyse sur la finance climat...

This rules the general signing-mode question prospectively. Child1584 will
implement the two generic modes and reconcile signature versus transcription
versus delegated-panel records. Drivers supply explicit delegation/campaign/scope
and provenance; they cannot self-grant authority. Plan amendments stay within
the approval perimeter or return to the author. Examples in the reply authorize
no pipeline creation, publishing, or paid spending. Pilot feasibility does not
become proof of general quality. No frozen pilot signature is rewritten.

The ruling is recorded, implementation/integration pending;1552 is not closed.
Other methodological holds and receiver-owned prompt pickup remain distinct.

## Author ruling: main-result choice (finding4)

The author approved the original-paper central-claim rule before package
inspection/execution: abstract/introduction, then supporting table or figure;
for equally ranked results, the driver prospectively motivates its choice
under a consistent cohort rule. The actual reply as relayed by /root was:

> D’accord. Ne pas hésiter à utiliser le advisor model, c’est une étape clé. Elsevier demande des key findings aux articles récents, penser à regarder en ligne si ils y sont.

Child1585 must actually consult a route advisor for guidance design and make
proportionate advisor use available for pivotal selection judgment. Optional
article-specific publisher Highlights/Key findings are original-paper evidence
to crosscheck, not a universal Elsevier requirement or an exception to blind
source restrictions. Missing/inaccessible highlights stay reported. Package
availability cannot choose the main result. This rules finding4 prospectively;
implementation/integration, other held findings, and1552 remain open.

## Author rulings: footnotes, dual reproduction, discrepancy impact

The author approved empirical results supporting the target claim regardless
of body/footnote location, excluding merely bibliographic remarks. Assertions
without numbers/code retain the existing probe rule. Actual reply relayed by/root:

> oui. Et de manière générale, tenir à la fois la reproduction computationnelle (implémentation, spécification) et la reproduction scientifique (argumentation, modèle, faits)

Footnote applicability is1586; the distinct broader intent is1587. Actually
consult an advisor for scientific-reproduction design. Preserve both axes,
argument/model/facts as well as implementation/specification, not DAG-only
causal review. No composite ACRe score, every-audit obligation, invented
subjective probabilities, or autonomous scientific signoff. Existing fairness
and approval of new empirical variants remain. Proposed checks are not evidence.

For finding10 the parent proposed preserving the observed computational
miss and separately assessing scientific impact. Assumed cause remains unknown;
documented typo or demonstrated numerical variation may support “scientific
result confirmed despite discrepancy” without erasure. Actual author reply:

> D’accord

Child1588 follows1587 design. No tolerance widening, miss-to-match relabeling,
size-alone harmlessness, or silent legacy rescore. All dialogue decisions for
findings4/5/10/12 are now received and supersede earlier held annotations
prospectively. Delivery/integration and receiver0009 pickup remain pending;
1552 completion is not inferred.
